WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
It's just you now.

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:02.600
You're alone.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.120
No one to turn to for help.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.820
Gotcha! The sport!

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:32.620
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:33.960
I'm Mike.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.720
I'm Sam. I'm Sean.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.060
And I'm Joe. I really gotcha guys, didn't I?

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.380
I was very surprised.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.100
Is that how you would read it though?

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:43.980
Is it more like, gotcha, right?

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.300
I feel like it's more like, gotcha.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:47.760
Yeah, that's what I got from it too.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.800
Gotcha! People in the United States call it paintball.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.680
Yeah. Is it called gotcha somewhere else?

00:00:54.680 --> 00:01:02.700
It's called gotcha the sport and I don't know if gotcha is like an actual sport or if it's just more like that they couldn't use paintball at the time or people wouldn't know what that was.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.180
So it's not just this game called gotcha.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.840
Someone calls paintball gotcha.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.620
Was paintball like popular at that time?

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.820
Both are irrelevant to my knowledge.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:17.000
Like, you know, like, gotcha I've never heard of before and paintball being popular.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.340
I only knew paintball like... Well, this game is what popularized paintball.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:23.100
I mean, I played paintball, but like, I don't think it was ever called gotcha.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.380
I think this is just them calling it gotcha.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.660
Right. So just the game is kind of...

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:29.560
Because they could have also called it capture the flag, the sport.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.140
Right. Yeah. You know, or capture the flag with guns.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.440
But I do definitely think that every game should be followed by the sport.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:36.760
Whatever the sport.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.020
Right. I'm actually going to...

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:46.260
Baseball. The sport. I think, I was thinking about that and I think that it's to let you know that it's just a game and that it's not actually, you know, shooting people.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.260
Okay. That's my take on it.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.420
Yeah, that makes sense. Like it's for sport.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.680
Yeah, it's like they're all, everyone's okay at the end of this.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:53.580
That's a good idea.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.320
Yeah, I like that. I also just think like...

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:03.180
We're just playing for flags. It's just necessary to have that be in the title because if you just call this gotcha, like that's weird.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.060
Right. Just picking that up on the shelves and being like, what do you got today?

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.520
Well, I could play gotcha.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.520
And they're like, oh, no, no, no, really, really.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.820
What do you have? I feel like it's just a bad title personally.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:12.900
It is a bad title.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.520
And that's how we're starting this episode.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.000
Because this is all about gotcha the sport.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:24.220
And that is, as we were alluding to, it's a light gun game where you also get to use the controller, which is kind of neat.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:30.020
And you're basically playing paintball as you go through like only three different stages.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.420
But I'm getting ahead of myself.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.100
But anyway, yeah. Okay.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.080
Four? Maybe there's three.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.520
Yeah, I was going to say, I'm pretty sure it's three.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:40.700
And I think before we get into like gameplay and stuff like that, let's just do first impressions.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:43.880
Because I feel like our audience isn't really familiar with this one either.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.400
It's being a later light gun game.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.300
So let's just talk about what grabbed us right from the start.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:57.800
Sam? So right from the start, I thought this feels more like an arcade style shooter, you know, with a gun.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:02.160
Where people just kind of pop out of different places and there's movement on it.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:03.780
Almost like an on-rails kind of shooter.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.940
But it's not on-rails because you're moving.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:10.880
But also that the art is really good, I thought, in this game.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.520
So those are really my first impressions.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:19.700
My first impression was, first of all, that I couldn't play this game the actual way.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.820
I had to emulate this because I don't have a CRT.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:27.200
And I thought that it was going to be completely unwieldy.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:35.360
But it actually seems to be even more, it's a better user experience if you just use like a PS4 controller

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:36.600
with a touchpad on the top.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.240
Because that's how I aimed.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:43.940
But yeah, I mean, it looks, the art style is fine.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.500
It's an interesting concept.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:52.060
But you're saying that's a better user experience than doing it, emulating it without the PS4 controller.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.420
Than emulating it without the PS4 controller.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.560
Because I did end up being able to play it with the actual zapper.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.220
And I think that was what kind of caught my attention first.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.060
Using the zapper while using the controller at the same time is something that we haven't done yet.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.580
Yeah. I don't even think any of the other games you use a controller even like to select things.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:12.880
Joe, was it you or Sam who suggested that in like one of our earlier episodes?

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:14.180
I was thinking about it. I can't remember.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.480
I think it was me with Gumshoe.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:22.400
I said that would be a cool thing to do with Gumshoe where you could jump with the A button and just shoot with the light gun.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:23.620
They took your advice. Yeah.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.420
I guess they're fans of the podcast.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:34.640
Yeah. But yeah, I mean really my initial impression was just kind of, I was very intrigued by that because it was something we haven't done yet before with a light gun.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:42.860
Okay. Yeah. And just to add in another way to play this game, I did emulate it because I also don't have access to a CRT in a New York City apartment.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.020
But just because there's no space.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:50.620
But I did try it with a Wiimote actually being able to hook up like the sensor bar and everything like that.

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:52.760
And that was interesting.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:56.180
I did also try it with just like mouse and keyboard.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.100
Yeah. That's always going to be terrible.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:04:59.780
Just to see what that's like.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:05.220
But I was actually surprised using mouse and keyboard that the hit boxes in this game are pretty weird.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:10.780
Yeah. It's not necessarily like if you get the guy right in the middle that it's going to register with a mouse click.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:16.660
I kept going for head shots and like I could see the blink for what the light gun is supposed to read.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.300
And the head isn't even in the hit box most of the time.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:22.960
Yeah. So I think for me that was like my first impression was just like, oh wow, hit boxes are weird.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:23.960
I'll have to get used to that.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:33.420
Because I did feel like in every other game, even including Gumshoe that we played, hit boxes felt very spot on because they were just kind of like the rectangle of the sprite.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:38.540
So anywhere within the sprite that you hit, that would also register a hit on the enemy.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.120
That's my thought on that.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.940
Real quick, I just also wanted to go over that this is an LJN game.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:47.640
Guys, any familiarity with LJN?

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.060
No. Not really, no.

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:53.500
Okay. Well, I'm sure NES, yes?

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.140
No. Okay, cool.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:56.220
Thank you for chiming in.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:10.400
I'm sure NES fans know that LJN makes just a series of terrible games that Cinemassacre, the angry video game nerd, he has gone on a whole rant about LJN.

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.680
Many people followed suit and stuff like that.

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:13.940
Here's what I'm going to say.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:20.780
Okay. Because I looked through the list and I've only ever played like four other LJN games other than now this one.

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:23.520
I'm going to give this like, I'm going to give them a chance.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:28.780
Okay. I'm not ready to say that their entire gamography on the NES is shit.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:31.760
You know, like I'll play through each one and make that decision myself.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:34.160
I'm not just going to say like, oh, that's a bad company.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:39.140
Whereas like we've seen now a few times where Bandai just can't get it together.

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:42.860
Yeah. You know, like Chubby Cherub and what else did they do?

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.140
They did one of the wrestling games, tag team wrestling.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.260
Yeah, they did Muscle. I thought they did Muscle.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.580
Oh, Muscle, yes. Muscle, yeah.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:49.800
Because of the license thing.

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:55.160
Yeah, yeah, yeah. So, you know, if Bandai got a chance from us, I feel like LJN should get one too.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.500
We don't judge.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:01.020
We should be judgment-free zone.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:04.580
Didn't you start this out by saying LJN is a company that makes bad games?

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:07.240
I said that they were known for that.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:12.260
Yeah, what's funny is LJN is defunct.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:18.200
Acclaim Entertainment, who also like was a subsidiary of them, they're defunct.

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:21.940
So no one has any like grandstand against me on this.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.580
You know, nobody can fight me on this.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.260
But you're going to give them a shot.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:26.420
The LJN fan club. To be clear.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:29.280
I'm going to give them the best shot I can.

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:32.980
And, you know, similar to you give the best shot you can in Gotcha.

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:34.960
The sport? The sport, yes.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:36.540
Not the saying. Not the word.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:41.700
Yeah. So before we get into the game, I was just, I was looking at the manual for this one.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.460
And there's nothing too interesting in there.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:50.140
But if you go to the manual section where it tells you like game is over and then gives you like the three scenarios.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.080
But it's actually four.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.380
Game is over when all blasters are lost.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:57.560
When the clock counts down to zero.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:00.940
When your flag is carried back to the opponent's base.

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:02.980
And when all.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:05.460
Yeah. I saw that.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:10.000
It's just like when all infinitively.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:12.860
When all anything happens.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.500
And that's like a bullet later on.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:15.780
It's like a weird format.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:17.660
Are we sure? It's not even indented in the same place.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.060
Are we sure that this isn't just like a bad scan?

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.900
Because I feel like we got the same scan.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:25.640
I've looked at two different scans of this manual and it has both.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:26.860
So I'm not.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.200
Yeah. It's very clean.

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:31.460
When all black have you around it.

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:38.220
Yeah. I'm not above thinking that LJ and a company that I'm going to give a chance would not make a mistake like that.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:42.620
They just came into like the copywriting room and it's like, okay, drop everything.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:43.580
Pencils down.

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:45.020
We have to ship this game.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:51.420
Pencils down. I was just making a room full of like thousands of people all writing the manual with pencil.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:53.280
And they all make the same mistake.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:55.620
Because they're going in unison.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.200
So they're all at the same point when they get the pencils down.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:26.640
I'm not.

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:52.480
Who thinks, and I'm gonna lean to Joe here,

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:56.920
who thinks that they could explain how to play Gotcha the Sport?

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:57.960
I can explain.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.020
Oh, great. I could have explained.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:01.280
I also could have explained.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:02.660
No, you couldn't.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:04.260
Not like this.

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:07.200
You've never explained like this before.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:08.540
Man, I'm really nervous now.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:12.240
So, Gotcha the Sport, you're playing with the light gun.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:14.880
So, it's very similar to any of the light gun games.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:16.020
You're shooting at your opponents.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:20.720
The only difference is you are scrolling to the right.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:23.800
Right. You're trying to get to the flag, which is all the way on the right.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:25.300
It's captured the flag.

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:27.460
So, you're running to get the flag.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.240
You shoot anyone that comes in your way before they shoot at you.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:33.700
And in the meantime, one of your opponents is trying to get your flag,

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:34.720
which you can see on your map.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.780
So, you watch as they run by.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:38.240
You basically just gotta shoot them when you go by.

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:42.480
It's pretty damn easy to make sure they don't get your flag.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.500
And then you run to the back, and then you win.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:48.900
You get their flag back to where your flag was, and now you win.

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:53.300
And it all happens on a side-scrolling thing.

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:56.140
Always in the first person. It's like first person, and you're strafing.

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:58.640
You in real life strafing sideways.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:10:59.920
And you also don't have any teammates.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:02.020
Thank you for bringing that up.

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:03.260
That was the weirdest thing.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:06.560
I remember like... I was trying to simulate all the other real wars on the NES,

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.440
where you're alone going in.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:12.560
Right. But because it's just a game where you move from left to right,

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:14.120
and you don't have any teammates,

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:17.460
essentially it's just a race for you to pick up the flag,

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:19.800
and then head back to where your base is,

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:21.620
and then somewhere in the middle meet the guy

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:24.100
who inadvertently must have taken your flag by now,

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:25.980
shoot him, and then just race back.

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:28.420
Yeah. It's pretty much just moving right to left.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:29.720
There's no strategy.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.160
There's no guarding your flag.

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:32.180
Well, you do go left to right later.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:33.840
Oh, that's true. Yeah, that's true.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.400
That changes it up a lot. That is true.

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:37.440
And you have... When you see someone on the screen,

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.820
a little target will come up under your screen

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:41.080
to show that they're aiming at you,

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:42.120
and that's when you know, like,

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.080
I better kill them, shoot them with a paintball

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:44.980
before they shoot me.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.200
Is that also necessary?

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:47.320
See, the thing is,

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:50.520
and I don't know if we were going to get to this later,

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:53.220
but this game is,

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:56.260
at least on the difficulty that I played at,

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:57.820
I didn't have to shoot anybody.

00:11:58.020 --> 00:11:59.680
It takes so long for them to aim.

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:01.340
I'm a beginner. I'm a beginner, yeah.

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:03.760
I'm a beginner. You cannot die if you keep moving.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:06.180
Okay. If you keep moving to the right I'm a beginner,

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.360
you will not fail,

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:09.360
and that's just like a whatever.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:11.300
Like, I'm glad that they include modes like that,

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:13.140
you know, for people who are bad at games.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:14.780
And then you can also try and rack up points

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:15.620
if that's what you're into.

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:16.920
But to Joe's point, yeah,

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:18.140
by the time you get to advanced,

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:20.960
that's like if you don't shoot them

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:22.340
within two or three seconds.

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:23.620
I feel like it's less than two seconds.

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:24.860
Wow. Yeah, I guess I'm over it.

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:25.760
I could be wrong, but...

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:27.140
No, I think I'm over it. Two seconds is a while.

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:28.580
That's like one, two.

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:30.600
Like, yeah, you got enough time to shoot down people.

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:33.320
I guess just with my thumb on the touchpad

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:35.240
acting as my reticle,

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:37.200
that was a bit more...

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:40.360
It would have taken me a lot of skill

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.240
to get everything in like less than a second.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:45.080
Right, yeah. But, you know,

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:46.480
since we're talking about the skill levels,

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.420
you have beginner, intermediate, and advanced,

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:50.100
and I welcome things like that.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:51.180
We really haven't had...

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:52.960
We've seen that the Japanese versions of games

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.080
sometimes get the easy and normal mode.

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:56.860
Most NES games that we've played

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:58.660
don't even give you difficulty options.

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:00.060
We get a lot of game A, game B,

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:01.020
which is really just...

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:03.140
Right. We haven't even seen game A or game B in a while.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.800
Yeah, yeah. That was like a Nintendo thing for the launch games.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.760
Yeah, yeah. You know, that really wasn't put into many games afterwards.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.140
And I just...

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.780
I welcome something like this at all turns

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:12.580
because it's also...

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:15.080
It's a game that isn't your typical game

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:16.240
because you're using the light gun

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:17.680
and the controller at the same time.

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.160
So you might need to start off

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:20.240
using something like beginner

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:21.260
just to get the... Learn the concept.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:23.540
Because the hitbox is so weird in this game

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:25.660
that I feel like if you jump right to advanced

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:27.600
just thinking like, oh, I'm good at Duck Hunt,

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.840
so I'll be good at this. It's like, it's not really the same.

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:31.660
Would you argue that...

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:33.180
Yeah, I mean, there's definitely...

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:34.080
It definitely feels...

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:35.560
To me, using the light gun,

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.640
I didn't notice what you guys were talking about.

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:39.800
Maybe because I'm not aiming as precisely

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:42.880
with the light gun, but I didn't notice that the hitboxes were off.

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:44.760
For me, it felt like if I missed,

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:46.600
it missed. And if I hit, it hit.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:50.480
But again, like I'm just aiming for like the chest

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:51.800
because it's like the biggest target

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:52.880
and I just assumed it didn't matter.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:54.980
But yeah, for the most part,

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:56.420
I felt like that, you know,

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.900
that aspect felt as good as Duck Hunt,

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:00.860
but then you're shooting with one hand

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:03.040
and you're controlling with the other.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:04.580
So that was like what made it a little different.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:07.840
And how did that feel with like using an actual,

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:09.920
you know, using the actual setup

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:12.080
of the NES controller and the light gun?

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.460
How did it feel to control both at the same time?

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:15.840
Honestly, I mean, since the controlling

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:18.360
on the actual like paddle

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:21.320
or whatever you call that is literally just left and right on the D-pad,

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:22.820
it was very...

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.700
It was pretty simple.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:26.180
It was not like it got that complicated,

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:27.800
but it was kind of weird to have like,

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:30.140
I don't know, even with, if you've played other light gun games,

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.500
you're probably used to using two hands,

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:32.600
kind of like, you know,

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.680
like you would hold like a rifle or something.

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:37.680
It was a little strange using one hand,

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:38.560
but it wasn't...

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.060
You got the flag in your other hands.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.660
That's true, yes. But what if you don't yet?

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:46.200
Sam, did you prefer being able to control

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:48.320
when you were moving throughout the stage

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.600
rather than clear all the enemies in this panel

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:52.900
and then we'll move you over to the next panel?

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:54.560
I kind of did it in chunks.

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:56.800
So I would kind of wait

00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:58.220
until there were a bunch of enemies in the screen

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:00.340
and then stop and kind of focus up on them

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:01.540
and then keep going.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:03.300
When I bet if I'd kept moving,

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:04.160
it probably would have been better,

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:05.840
but I think aiming was a little bit easier

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:07.020
when you were stationary.

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:08.340
At least I found that.

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:11.240
So... And it sounds like,

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:12.900
Sean, your strategy was just more like

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:13.840
keep moving forward.

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:16.060
I mean, not saying that's what I did.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:18.080
I just realized that after playing

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.420
that, oh, I could have just let this all happen

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:21.460
and just keep going.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.960
But no, I stopped every once in a while

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:25.060
when there were a bunch of enemies

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:27.280
or I see the flag getting ran back

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:28.660
to the other side.

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:31.340
So yeah, I kind of did it the way that Sam did.

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:34.300
And one thing to give this game credit for

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:37.040
is that even though there's only three stages,

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.320
they got pretty creative with those stages

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:42.380
and where enemies land and stuff like that.

00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:44.640
Like, I was really surprised in the forest

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.160
when the first guy who killed me

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:47.420
was hidden behind a waterfall.

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:50.300
You don't see that coming.

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:53.400
And then all of a sudden you're like, oh yeah, they can be anywhere on the stage.

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:56.180
They don't have to just spawn in the usual places.

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:57.580
Some of the people that are laying on their stomach

00:15:57.580 --> 00:15:59.020
are kind of hard to see at first two

00:15:59.020 --> 00:15:59.980
and then someone's aiming at you

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.000
and you're like, where is that guy?

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:03.380
Yeah. But I did laugh, speaking of the stages,

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:06.880
I did laugh a little bit at the level of specificity.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:08.800
Yes, yeah. Well, that's what I was about to get into.

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:09.840
So please get into that.

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.220
Because the first stage is forest.

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:12.700
You're just in a forest.

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:15.620
You don't need to know exactly which forest.

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:17.480
Then the second stage is Bronx.

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:20.660
The Bronx. But they also call it the ghetto,

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.460
which is really like a backhand to the Bronx.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:24.560
Oh, wow. Where do they call it that?

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:28.440
On screen? I think it's in the manual.

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:29.760
Is it not? It could be.

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:31.000
You just had the one spot I'm looking at

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.160
that says Bronx. Yeah.

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:34.020
Yeah, I didn't see ghetto, but...

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:36.320
Maybe, okay. It's not Freudian.

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:37.820
But it's also... No, it is just weird, right?

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:39.780
It's like the selection of stages is like,

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:41.980
okay, so naturally you would start in a forest, right?

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.360
That's like this game's Green Hill Zone, right?

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:47.640
Whatever. And then the Bronx is just like,

00:16:47.720 --> 00:16:50.600
now we're just out in the open playing paintball.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:55.060
Right. Like in the city. With these giant muscular dudes with mohawks also.

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:58.080
Yeah, they're punks. They're not even like people who represent the Bronx.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:00.220
They're like, oh no, we're just playing paintball though.

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.460
Right. But then the third stage is just winter.

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:05.260
Yeah. It's not even a place now.

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:06.580
It's just a season that you're in.

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:08.540
Which they got creative with again,

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:10.080
with the snow and stuff like that.

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:12.800
Right. And, you know, having different vantage points for the enemies.

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:14.860
But it's still just bottomed my mind

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:17.880
that they thought that like winter would be the ultimate end stage.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:19.480
Like, you know, like, oh, where do we go next?

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:20.640
Back to forest.

00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:24.720
So the introduction of the manual has this excerpt.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.500
Whether you're in the dense green woods,

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.180
the steamy urban ghetto,

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.500
or the snow-covered winter forest,

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:33.240
there's only one thing on your mind.

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:36.720
Survival. So, yeah, they call it a steamy urban ghetto,

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.300
which is, I guess, like, not a very nice way

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:40.760
to talk about the Bronx.

00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:42.080
I always believed in you, Sean.

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:43.480
I knew you wouldn't just make that up.

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:45.980
Yeah, no, all of this is,

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:47.540
all of this is strange because it's,

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:51.920
where is just regular paintball locations?

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:54.840
Yeah, yeah. I mean, when I used to play when I was a kid,

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:59.320
we just had this weird, like, unused plot of forest.

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:01.080
Right, but I wouldn't have minded even, like,

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:03.000
castle or something, you know?

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.240
Yeah, it's a video game.

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:05.900
Let your imagination run wild, you know?

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:07.740
Yeah, yeah. Instead, it's like...

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:10.580
Space paint. Yeah, it could only ever happen in three locations.

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:12.220
Everybody knows paintball only ever happens

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:13.480
in the winter, the forest, or the Bronx.

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:17.920
Yeah, the Bronx. In the forest or the winter forest.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:19.780
They didn't even think to do that.

00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:21.360
No, that's what it says in the manual.

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:22.960
Yeah, it says it when Sean does.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:25.800
A winter forest. I just meant, like, a version of the forest

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:26.980
that's just covered in stuff.

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:27.860
Or the city forest. That's just winter.

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:29.720
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:32.920
Where was the Bronx forest crossover we were all waiting for?

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:34.740
It's like place, time, and concept.

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:36.400
And if you're wondering why we're talking so much

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:37.940
about the stages, it's because we pretty much

00:18:37.940 --> 00:18:40.120
run out of things to talk about when it comes to this game.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:41.640
This game does not offer a lot.

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:44.880
Well, okay. It gives you...

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:49.260
No. There's this thing...

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:52.520
We mentioned that you can tell when people aim at you.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:54.380
That's cool, right?

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:56.300
I still wasn't sure until that moment

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:57.740
if you were doing a bit there or not.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.760
No. There's a song that plays also when they aim at you.

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:03.520
Yeah. There were three different songs, actually,

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:04.960
that I thought were interesting.

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:06.440
No, it went in love.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:07.840
I thought it was interesting. The song changed.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:09.100
Like you said, when someone's aiming at you,

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:12.200
it's a different song. When your opponent has your flag,

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:15.340
it's a different song. And then when nobody has your flag...

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:16.240
Well, the only thing I don't like

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:17.960
is that when you have their flag,

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:19.080
but they have your flag,

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:21.940
you hear the song of your flag being stolen.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:23.200
You don't get to hear a song

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:24.320
for you having a flag.

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:26.020
Yeah, there's no success. And it's like,

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.060
well, I'll only ever get to stop hearing this music

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:30.660
once I finally cross paths with this guy

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:31.600
and shoot him immediately.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:34.600
Yeah. That's my problem with this game

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:38.480
is that it's just one character going one way,

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:40.160
another character going another way.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.000
Eventually, they'll find a middle point,

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:43.580
which might not necessarily be the middle.

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:45.740
Like some characters move slower than us or whatever,

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:47.580
but eventually there's just going to be a point

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.260
where the only thing you have to do

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:50.820
is just shoot the guy with the flag

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:51.680
and then keep moving.

00:19:51.680 --> 00:19:54.500
There's never anything about like planning

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.580
when to take down the other enemies.

00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:59.080
So that leads me to a question I kind of have.

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:02.240
So what do you think could have made this a better game?

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:06.300
Like not like what would be a modern paintball game,

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:09.380
but what would be a better NES light gun paintball game?

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:11.640
What would they have to do?

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:12.840
I almost think...

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:14.960
So I can't remember if we talked about this

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:16.060
in an earlier game,

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:17.340
similar to what Sam said earlier,

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.820
but like I almost want one person

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.040
to be controlling the guy

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:23.060
and the other person to be covering them

00:20:23.060 --> 00:20:24.940
with the light gun. I almost feel like that would be...

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:28.720
That'd be cool. Some game where even if the platforming is almost...

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:30.640
Even if the platforming is like a Super Mario game

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:33.060
and you can jump on enemies and whatnot,

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.420
but then maybe there's some enemies

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:36.600
that only the gun can take out,

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.160
some enemies only the character can take out,

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:39.280
and some that cross over.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:40.580
And then you can kind of like plan and be like...

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:42.200
That is an idea. I never thought about something like that.

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:44.880
You can be like, all right, so you cover this area,

00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:47.740
I'll get this area, whatever. And that's a cool co-op game.

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:49.420
And they include an entire map

00:20:49.420 --> 00:20:51.460
with like where your flag is on that map

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:53.420
and where their flag is and stuff like that.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:55.820
Why not just also include points

00:20:55.820 --> 00:20:58.360
for where all of everybody is on the screen

00:20:58.360 --> 00:20:59.960
and track them all as if like,

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:01.740
you know, here's where your teammates are.

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:03.340
I'm assuming in my version of this game

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:06.060
that I have teammates. Here's where their people are.

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:08.140
And then keeping in mind that like,

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:11.540
oh, right now there's only one guy guarding my flag,

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:13.900
so I should send people that way

00:21:13.900 --> 00:21:15.420
or send myself that way,

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:18.620
have my AI people focus on getting the flag.

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.400
Maybe that's something you could even do

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:22.280
by like hitting the start button.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:25.060
And like, I guess I'm going the opposite of Joe's thing

00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:27.360
because I'm almost saying if you're going to make us use the controller,

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:29.300
just make us use the whole controller.

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:31.460
Don't worry about just the left and right thing.

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:33.980
Like I'm saying... Oh man, I can see this being...

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:34.980
Well, continue your thought.

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:36.120
I just think like get kind of cool with it.

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:37.480
Like you have A and B

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:39.660
almost be like commands for your team squad.

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:41.720
Like B could be like play more defensive.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:44.160
A could be get more aggressive towards their flag.

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:46.360
This is a much more complex game now.

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:47.380
Oh, absolutely. Yeah.

00:21:47.560 --> 00:21:50.280
But I also just think that it's a better game

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:54.000
because I think that they left a lot of the structure there.

00:21:54.220 --> 00:21:55.680
Like I said, the enemies are really cool

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:57.320
how they hide behind things

00:21:57.320 --> 00:21:58.780
and that they took the time to,

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:00.000
even if there's only three levels,

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:01.800
that the three levels act differently.

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:04.480
That's cool. But there's just not enough going on

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:05.520
with the gameplay loop

00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:07.340
that doesn't stop me from just going like,

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:09.040
all right, just keep moving right,

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:10.700
keep moving right, up, there's a guy, shoot him,

00:22:10.820 --> 00:22:12.440
keep moving right, there's a guy, shoot him,

00:22:12.780 --> 00:22:15.640
grab the flag, and then wait till I run into the other guy.

00:22:15.780 --> 00:22:16.960
I think that if you keep the light gun

00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:18.080
as a part of it, though,

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:21.920
the amount of use you're getting

00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:22.880
out of the controller

00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:24.100
is really going to hamper

00:22:24.100 --> 00:22:25.500
your light gun experience

00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:27.540
because you get, at one point it seems like

00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:28.740
you're going to have to put it down

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:30.840
and issue commands or something

00:22:30.840 --> 00:22:31.800
on the controller.

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:33.280
What if you... I almost imagine it,

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:34.960
sorry, but I almost imagine it like,

00:22:35.040 --> 00:22:37.080
you know, you got your gun out like this

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:38.580
and then in your other hand,

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:40.500
you're almost, you're holding it almost like a walkie,

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:42.140
you know, and then you're just using

00:22:42.140 --> 00:22:43.420
like your pinky

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:44.980
and ring finger

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:47.600
to execute the B&A commands

00:22:47.600 --> 00:22:48.700
and using,

00:22:48.740 --> 00:22:49.860
you know, using your index

00:22:49.860 --> 00:22:50.860
for the left and right.

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:52.120
Idea. Okay.

00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:53.980
Like gun in one hand,

00:22:54.220 --> 00:22:55.640
power glove in the other hand.

